{"id":"n-20261027-yopfc6","category":"business","display_title":"Anthropic Files For Massive IPO","display_title_he":"אנתרופיק מגישה בקשה להנפקה ענקית","short_summary":"Artificial intelligence developer Anthropic has filed for a public offering on the Nasdaq, with market estimates suggesting a valuation reaching up to two trillion dollars.","english_level":"C1","words":497,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/economy/article/b1tuma22gl","title":"2 טריליון דולר: אנתרופיק בדרך לאחת ההנפקות הגדולות בהיסטוריה","published_at":"2026-10-26T13:24:57.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3873835","title":"שווי של 2 טריליון דולר: אנתרופיק בדרך להנפקה הגדולה בהיסטוריה","published_at":"2026-10-26T17:25:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-26T13:24:57.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-27T06:26:13.058Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Anthropic, the artificial intelligence company behind the Claude chatbot, has officially filed for an initial public offering on the Nasdaq exchange under the ticker symbol ANT. Four months after submitting confidential documents to the US Securities and Exchange Commission, the enterprise published a public prospectus. Market reports indicate that the upcoming offering could potentially value the enterprise at up to two trillion dollars and raise approximately one hundred billion dollars, positioning it to surpass the record set earlier this year by Elon Musk's SpaceX and become one of the largest market debuts in financial history. The process is expected to be led by major investment banks including Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley, alongside roughly twenty other banks.","The regulatory filings provided investors with their first official glimpse into the company's financial status. During the first half of 2026, Anthropic generated 16.29 billion dollars in revenue. However, the firm also recorded a net loss exceeding eighty billion dollars during the same period, with specific figures noting a net loss of 80.75 billion dollars. Company representatives explained that these losses are largely attributable to the massive computing infrastructure expenses required to train and develop advanced models, alongside accounting items that do not involve actual cash outflows and therefore do not reflect actual cash flow.","Founded in 2021 by a group of former researchers who left OpenAI, including CEO Dario Amodei and President Daniela Amodei, the enterprise has expanded rapidly within a fiercely competitive sector. If completed as planned, Anthropic will become the first company focused on advanced AI models to trade publicly. Data from the fintech firm Ramp indicated that by September, nearly forty-four percent, specifically 43.8 percent, of American businesses utilized Anthropic services, surpassing OpenAI. Furthermore, research firm Sensor Tower estimated that Claude reached over sixty-seven million monthly active users during the third quarter of 2026, marking a substantial increase compared to the 9.4 million users from the previous year.","The public offering arrives amid an unprecedented investment boom across the technology industry, with major players like Meta, Google, OpenAI, and Anthropic spending billions on artificial intelligence infrastructure. Research firm Gartner projects that global spending on artificial intelligence, including services, software, and infrastructure, will reach 3.6 trillion dollars by 2027, compared to 1.8 trillion dollars in 2025. This rapid evolution includes tools like Claude Code introduced in early 2025, and the Cowork agent, which helped accelerate the shift from chatbots to agents while shaking software stocks. Competitors have also pushed forward, with OpenAI launching Codex and a multi-step agent called ChatGPT Work.","Despite the commercial growth, Anthropic has also found itself at the center of discussions regarding safety and development pace. Last month, CEO Dario Amodei publicly urged the industry to slow down its momentum, allowing safety research, regulation, and standard compliance adequate time to keep pace with rapid innovations. This statement followed the resignation of an employee over existential AI fears and industry reports regarding models breaching other corporate systems during experiments, creating a central test of investor confidence as Wall Street grows increasingly concerned over AI infrastructure returns."],"facts":[{"fact":"Anthropic has filed for an initial public offering on the Nasdaq exchange under the ticker symbol ANT.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Market estimates suggest the IPO could value the company at up to 2 trillion dollars and raise around 100 billion dollars.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"In the first half of 2026, Anthropic reported 16.3 billion dollars in revenue and a net loss exceeding 80 billion dollars, largely driven by computing infrastructure costs.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Monthly active users for Claude grew to over 67 million in the third quarter of 2026, up from 9.4 million a year prior.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"CEO Dario Amodei recently called for the AI industry to slow down to allow safety research and regulation to catch up.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Anthropic","lemma":"Anthropic","pos":"PROPN","he":"אנתרופיק","name":"true"},{"text":"artificial","lemma":"artificial","pos":"ADJ","he":"מלאכותי","name":false},{"text":"intelligence","lemma":"intelligence","pos":"NOUN","he":"בינה","name":false},{"text":"company","lemma":"company","pos":"NOUN","he":"חברה","name":false},{"text":"behind","lemma":"behind","pos":"ADP","he":"מאחורי","name":false},{"text":"Claude","lemma":"Claude","pos":"PROPN","he":"קלוד","name":"true"},{"text":"chatbot","lemma":"chatbot","pos":"NOUN","he":"צ'טבוט","name":false},{"text":"officially","lemma":"officially","pos":"ADV","he":"רשמית","